
  # Performance / Explain

   Query and what it does :-

   Show the query plan — is it using an index or scanning the whole table?
   EXPLAIN SELECT * FROM orders WHERE customer_id = 5;

   Plan plus actual execution timing ->
   EXPLAIN ANALYZE SELECT ...; (Postgres)

   Red flag — full table scan, usually means a missing index->
   Look for type: ALL (MySQL) or Seq Scan (Postgres) in the plan

   List existing indexes on a table->
   SHOW INDEXES FROM orders; (MySQL) / \d orders (psql)
